use std
into forms.amni

Namespace grow; imports math, vec, grow.grow. Organic forms built from the `grow` verbs (`rnd`, `range`, `vary`, `pick`, `noise`, `fbm`, `ridged`, `vert`, `tri`, `quad`, `tube`, `revolve`, `ico`, `normals`, `move`, `spin`, `scale`, `fit`, `bounds`, `unit`, `basis`, `rot`, `tint`, `mixc`, `pos`, `nrm`, `col`, `set_pos`, `set_col`, the arrays `P`, `N`, `C`, `I`, `S`, `FORKS` and the constants `GOLDEN` and `PI2`; all already exist and must not be defined here). Every form takes a base point `b double3` (the middle of its footprint, Y up) and a `size real` in meters, and appends to the current mesh. Colors are linear RGB.

Ids, the rule every block follows: P, N and C hold three floats per vertex and I three ids per triangle, so their lengths are never ids. A part's first vertex is `vcount()` and its first triangle is `tcount()`, taken before building it; loops over a part's vertices run from that first vertex to `vcount()`, over its triangles from that first triangle to `tcount()`, and over the points in S by its pairs or triples. `normals` always gets both the first vertex and the first triangle. Every surface of revolution (mushroom cap, cactus body, flower disc) calls `revolve`, passing its profile as a flat list of reals in (radius, height) pairs from the top down with a zero radius at each closed end, so the shape is closed; never write another lathe.

`ground(v0 int, b double3, size real)` places the part that starts at vertex v0: `fit` it about the point (b.x, its lowest y, b.z) to size, then `move` it up or down so its lowest point is at b.y.

`phyllo(n int, spacing real)` clears S and appends n points (x, z pairs, relative to the origin): point i at radius `spacing * sqrt(i + 0.5)` and angle `i * GOLDEN`.

`scatter(cx real, cz real, radius real, count int, gap real)` clears S and appends up to count (x, z) points inside the disc: up to `count * 37` tries of a uniform point in the disc (radius `radius * sqrt(rnd())`, angle `PI2 * rnd()`), keeping a point only when it is at least gap from every kept point, stopping once count are kept.

`on_surface(t0 int, count int, min_up real)` clears S and appends count (x, y, z) points on triangles t0 to the end whose unit face normal has a y of at least min_up, chosen with probability proportional to area (cumulative areas, a binary search with rnd()) at a uniform point inside the triangle (two rnd() values folded back into the triangle when their sum passes 1). Nothing is appended when no triangle qualifies.

`leaf(b double3, dir double3, up double3, len real, width real, curl real, fold real, segs int, c double3) int` is a single blade surface; returns its first vertex id. d is `unit(dir)`, side is `unit(cross(d, up))`, n is `cross(side, d)`. The midrib point at u in [0, 1] is b plus len times (d times `sin(curl * u) / curl` minus n times `(1 - cos(curl * u)) / curl`), using d times u and no droop when curl is below 1e-4; its forward direction at u is d rotated about side by minus `curl * u`. Half width at u is `0.5 * width * pow(sin(PI * pow(u, 0.7)), 0.8)`. Build segs plus one rows of three vertices (left edge, midrib, right edge, across = -1, 0, 1); a vertex sits at the midrib point plus side times across times half width plus the local normal times `fold * |across| * half width`. Join rows with quads facing the local normal, then `normals` over the new part. Colors: c times 0.82 on the midrib and `tint(c, 0.07)` at the edges, lighter toward the tip by up to 15 %.

`blade(b double3, lean double3, h real, w real, c double3) int` is a grass blade of 4 segments: point at t = k / 4 is b plus up times `h * t` plus lean times `h * t * t`; two vertices per row (width `w * (1 - t)` across the direction perpendicular to lean and up), one tip vertex; quads and the tip triangle face the side `cross(lean_side, up)` points to; `normals` over it; color from `c * 0.55` at the base to `tint(c, 0.1)` at the tip.

`tuft(b double3, size real, c double3)` grows `17 + pick(11)` blades inside radius `0.35 * size`: each base offset by `scatter`-free random polar offsets, height `vary(size, 0.3)`, width `0.035 * size`, lean a horizontal unit vector at a random angle times `range(0.15, 0.55)`, so the tuft is about size tall.

`rock(b double3, size real)` is a closed boulder: `ico(b, 1, 3)`; for each new vertex with unit direction u, radius `1 + 0.35 * fbm(u * 1.7 + o, 5) + 0.15 * (ridged(u * 3.1 + o, 3) - 0.5)` where o is a random offset (three `range(0, 100)`), then y times `vary(0.72, 0.15)` and y raised to at least -0.55 (flat bottom); `normals`; color mixes stone grey (0.42, 0.40, 0.37) and warm brown (0.45, 0.36, 0.27) by `0.5 + 0.5 * fbm(u * 2.3 + o, 3)`, darkened by 30 % where the radius is below 1 and lightened 12 % where the normal's y is above 0.6, then `tint` 0.04; finally `fit(v0, b lowered to the rock's lowest point, size)` and `move` so the lowest point sits at b.

`shell(b double3, size real)` is a closed sea shell (Raup's coiling): turns `range(4.5, 7)`, whorl growth `w = vary(1.8, 0.12)`, k = `ln(w) / PI2`, height ratio `h = range(0.9, 2.7)` (low snail to tall whelk), tube ratio `q = range(0.38, 0.5)`. Path point at theta from 0 to `PI2 * turns` in `turns * 27` steps: R = `exp(k * theta)`; position (R cos theta, minus h times R, R sin theta); tube radius q times R; color mixes cream (0.86, 0.78, 0.64) and brown (0.45, 0.25, 0.13) by `0.5 + 0.5 * sin(theta * 3 + 2 * noise(...))` banding, then tint 0.04. `tube` with 17 sides and caps; then `fit` to size with its lowest point moved to b.

`mushroom(b double3, size real)` builds a closed stem and a closed cap. Stem: `tube` along 5 points rising `0.62 * size` with a small random bend, radius from `0.11 * size` at the base to `0.075 * size` at the top, color (0.88, 0.85, 0.78) tinted, 13 sides, caps. Cap: `revolve` around the stem top with segs 27, ribs 0, wobble 0.04, profile (top to bottom) pole at height `0.2 * size` over the stem top, then dome points at radius fractions 0.35, 0.62, 0.82, 0.96, 1.0 of cap radius `vary(0.42, 0.15) * size` dropping to the rim, then the underside back in at radius `0.3` and `0.12` of the cap radius slightly above the rim, then a pole on the axis just below the rim. Red toadstool (cap (0.62, 0.07, 0.05) with white spots where `noise(position * 7 / size)` is above 0.35) on a coin flip, otherwise brown (0.42, 0.28, 0.16); underside gills colored (0.83, 0.76, 0.66). Fit to size, base at b.

`cactus(b double3, size real)` is a closed ribbed column: `revolve` at b with segs 37, ribs `9 + 2 * pick(3)`, rib_depth 0.3, wobble 0.02, profile from a top pole at height size, rounding down through radius fractions 0.5, 0.85, 1.0 of `0.16 * size`, straight to the ground at radius `0.17 * size`, then a bottom pole at height 0; green (0.20, 0.42, 0.18) tinted. Then 0 to 2 arms (`pick(3)`): each a capped `tube` of 7 points that leaves the trunk sideways at height `range(0.3, 0.6) * size`, bends and rises to about `0.75 * size`, radius `0.1 * size`, 13 sides.

`succulent(b double3, size real)` is a rosette: `phyllo(37, 0.06 * size)`; for each point i, a thick leaf (`leaf` with segs 5, fold 0.45) from b pointing outward along the point's direction, rising more steeply toward the center (pitch from 75 degrees for the first point to 15 degrees for the last), length `vary(0.5 * size * (0.45 + 0.55 * i / 37), 0.1)`, width 0.45 of its length, curl -0.6; blue green (0.36, 0.55, 0.47) blending to dusty pink (0.72, 0.47, 0.50) at the tips.

`flower(b double3, size real)` is a stem, two leaves and a head. Stem: `tube` of 7 points rising to size with a small bend, radius `0.018 * size`, green, 7 sides, caps. Two leaves on the stem at heights 0.25 and 0.45 of size, opposite sides, length `0.3 * size`. Head at the stem top, facing up and a little sideways: petals count chosen from 5, 8, 13, 21, each a `leaf` (segs 7, curl 0.5, fold 0.15) of length `0.22 * size` and width `0.09 * size` spread evenly around the head's axis, color one of yellow (0.95, 0.80, 0.12), white (0.93, 0.92, 0.88), violet (0.45, 0.25, 0.70) or red (0.80, 0.12, 0.15). Disc: a `revolve` dome of radius `0.07 * size` (segs 17) in brown (0.30, 0.18, 0.05), then `phyllo(89, 0.0065 * size)` florets, each a 4-sided pyramid of height `0.008 * size` on the dome in dark gold (0.55, 0.40, 0.05).

`branch(p double3, d double3, len real, r0 real, r1 real, depth int, maxd int, kind int)` grows one branch and its children (kind 0 broadleaf tree, 1 bush, 2 coral). Path of 5 points from p along d, each later point nudged by `0.12 * len * fbm` sideways and, for kind 0 and 1, a slight upward pull; radii linear from r0 to r1; bark color (0.30, 0.22, 0.15) for trees and bushes, coral (0.95, 0.45, 0.35) tinted for coral; `tube` with 7 sides (5 for depth 3 and deeper), caps. When depth is below maxd: child count 2 or 3 (3 with probability 0.4); weights `range(0.6, 1)`; child start radius `r1 * sqrt(weight / total weight)`; append to FORKS the pair (r1, sum of the children's squared start radii); each child direction is d tilted away by `range(25, 45)` degrees (`range(15, 30)` for coral) about a perpendicular axis turned by `GOLDEN` per child and a random offset, for kind 0 and 1 blended 20 % toward straight up; child length `len * vary(0.72, 0.1)` (0.8 for coral), end radius 0.62 of its start radius (0.8 for coral). Otherwise, at the tip: kind 0 adds 7 leaves (length `0.11` of the tree size kept in a module var `TREE_SIZE`, segs 4, curl 0.4) around the tip direction in greens (0.20, 0.42, 0.12) tinted 0.12; kind 1 adds 11 smaller leaves; kind 2 adds nothing (the cap rounds it).

`tree(b double3, size real)` sets TREE_SIZE, calls `branch` from b straight up with length `0.34 * size`, radius `0.045 * size` to `0.033 * size`, maxd 5, kind 0, then `fit` to size with its lowest point at b. `bush(b double3, size real)` is the same with three trunks spread 25 degrees from vertical, length `0.3 * size`, radius `0.025 * size`, maxd 3, kind 1. `coral(b double3, size real)` is branch kind 2 with five upward starts spread 30 degrees, length `0.25 * size`, radius `0.05 * size`, maxd 4.

`pine(b double3, size real)` is a conifer: trunk `tube` of 7 points straight up to size, radius `0.035 * size` tapering to `0.003 * size`, 7 sides, caps, bark color. Whorls every `0.07 * size` from 0.22 to 0.95 of the height: 5 branches per whorl at angles turned by `GOLDEN` per whorl, length `0.38 * size * (1 - height fraction) + 0.04 * size`, drooping 12 to 25 degrees below horizontal; each branch a capped 3-point tube (radius `0.006 * size`, 5 sides) with 7 needle tufts along it, each tuft 5 `leaf`s (segs 2, width `0.008 * size`, length `0.06 * size`, curl 0) fanned around the branch; dark green (0.08, 0.22, 0.10) tinted 0.1.

`fern(b double3, size real)` has 7 fronds radiating from b at even angles plus jitter. Each frond spine is a capped `tube` of 9 points (radius `0.006 * size`, 5 sides) rising at 55 to 70 degrees then arching outward and down (curl over its length `range(0.9, 1.3)` radians), length `vary(size, 0.1)`. Along the spine 17 pairs of pinnae, one each side, `leaf` with segs 4, fold 0.2, curl 0.3, length `0.26 * frond length * sin(PI * pow(t, 0.8))` (t the place along the spine, from 0.12 to 0.97), width 0.22 of its length, pointing out sideways and slightly forward; green (0.15, 0.40, 0.10) tinted 0.08, younger (lighter) toward the tip.

`brain_coral(b double3, size real)` is a closed dome: `ico(b, 1, 4)`, radius `1 + 0.07 * sin(23 * noise(u * 1.3 + o))` along each unit direction u, y raised to at least -0.35; `normals`; color from deep (0.55, 0.42, 0.20) in grooves to light (0.85, 0.75, 0.48) on ridges by the same sine; fit to size with the lowest point at b.

`moss(b double3, size real)` is a `rock` of size whose vertices with a normal y above 0.3 are recolored toward moss green (0.20, 0.38, 0.08) by `smoothstep(0.3, 0.7, normal y) * (0.6 + 0.4 * fbm(position * 4 / size, 3))`, then `on_surface` over the rock's triangles with 700 points and min_up 0.45, each point getting a tiny `blade` (height `vary(0.05, 0.4) * size`, width `0.008 * size`, random lean `range(0.1, 0.4)`) in moss green (0.25, 0.45, 0.10) tinted 0.15.

`KINDS` is the list "rock", "shell", "mushroom", "cactus", "succulent", "flower", "tuft", "tree", "pine", "bush", "fern", "coral", "brain_coral", "moss". `make(kind, s, size)` (kind a read-only byte slice, s an int, size a real; returns a bool) calls `clear()`, `seed(s)`, builds that kind at the origin with that size, then `fit(0, origin, size)` so its largest side is exactly the asked size, and returns true, or returns false for an unknown kind.
